## Core Java Memory Management Principles

### 1. JVM Memory Areas and Management

#### Heap Memory Structure
```java
// Understanding heap generations
// Young Generation: Eden + Survivor Spaces (S0, S1)
// Old Generation: Tenured Space
// Metaspace: Class metadata (Java 8+)

// JVM tuning parameters
// -Xmx4g -Xms2g                    // Heap size
// -XX:NewRatio=3                   // Old/Young generation ratio
// -XX:MaxMetaspaceSize=256m        // Metaspace limit
// -XX:MaxDirectMemorySize=1g       // Direct memory limit
```

#### Garbage Collection Algorithms
```java
// G1 GC (recommended for most applications)
// -XX:+UseG1GC -XX:MaxGCPauseMillis=200 -XX:G1HeapRegionSize=16m

// ZGC (ultra-low latency, Java 11+)
